\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Four uniform steps at $\tau = 0.19$ ($V = 0.144$). At the first step the weight $0.75$ falls on $\bm  {x}_t = \bm  {x}_1$, so $\bm  {x}_{t_{N-1}} = 0.25\,\mathbb  {E}[\bm  {x}_0\mid \bm  {x}_1] + 0.75\,\bm  {x}_1 + 0.165\,\bm  {z}$. Uniform steps in $t$ give equal ratios $r$ in the middle of the ladder.}}{11}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:i2sb_run}{{1}{11}{Four uniform steps at $\tau = 0.19$ ($V = 0.144$). At the first step the weight $0.75$ falls on $\x _t = \x _1$, so $\x _{t_{N-1}} = 0.25\,\E [\x _0\mid \x _1] + 0.75\,\x _1 + 0.165\,\zz $. Uniform steps in $t$ give equal ratios $r$ in the middle of the ladder}{table.1}{}}
